+# Lessons from past consultations
+
+- An exam showed a deficit (bilateral decreased hearing) that the patient said they had not noticed.
+  The doctor went with the patient's report, ignored the finding, and submitted a neighbouring
+  diagnosis that does not include that deficit. Lesson: never explain away an abnormal objective
+  finding because the history did not mention it. Order the confirmatory test and let the finding
+  decide between closely related diagnoses.
+- The doctor spent several requests asking again for exam details that the record had already said
+  were not available. Once a result says "not in the record", use the remaining budget on other
+  discriminating exams or tests instead.
